    "comment": "Porcelain greenware. Molds and crucibles are deliberately absent: they are fire-clay-only for the same reason porcelain would be wrong in them. Every entry below fires to shards except a perfectly sealed beehive (0 open doors) \u2014 porcelain needs an even, fully oxidising soak, and the pit kiln cannot give it one at all. The '0' beehive entry doubles as the canonical perfect-firing output that the Parcel 3 updraft kiln reads off the block, so the mapping is never duplicated in C#.",
